title: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tiddlers/sigil-scale
tags: $:/tags/Global lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/SharktoothSigil
lar-kind: ordered-scale
lar-pono-uri: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/scale
lar-pattern: <<~\s*scale\s+name=`([\w-]+)`(?:\s+ranks=`([^`]*)`)?\s*>>
lar-example: <<~ scale name=`organ` ranks=`a ~ one -> b ~ two`>>
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<!-- scale — an ORDERED SCALE and the ranks it carries. A SCALE is the thing; RANKS are what it
     holds, joined by an arrow INSIDE the value with a gloss apiece:

         <<~ scale name=`organ` ranks=`mempalace ~ FIRST -> structurepalace ~ structure plane`>>

     The boot seed held this shape before the sigil did — `\procedure scale(name ranks)` called as
     `<<scale name=`levels` ranks=`rank-1@0..4 -> rank-2@5..8 -> …`>>`. A name, then a ranked body.

     THE CHAIN RIDES TICKED. It carries `->`, `~`, colons and prose; one pair of ticks makes the whole
     chain ONE value, and the ranks read within it. An arrow INSIDE a value stays; an arrow BETWEEN
     two values has no place in a call. -->

\procedure ~scale(name:"" ranks:"")
<span class="lar-scale"><<name>> <<ranks>></span>
\end
